= Preprint — Technical =

Preprints are versioned research objects. Reliable scholarly systems should preserve identifiers and relationships among preprints, revised versions, accepted manuscripts, versions of record, corrections, and withdrawals so readers can distinguish publication state.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* preprint ≠ peer-reviewed article
* public availability ≠ peer-review certification
* preprint version ≠ final version necessarily

== References ==
* NIH/National Library of Medicine, PMC Preprint Pilot, “What is a preprint?”, current resource.
* UNESCO, ''Recommendation on Open Science'' (2021), preprints distinguished from final peer-reviewed publications.
* Crossref metadata schema/documentation, preprint registration and relations.
